{
    "attributes": {
        "action": "Amend the Children Act to make parental responsibility enforceable",
        "additional_details": "Parental responsibility should mean enforceable duties to the child, not just legal rights. Some parents retain rights, seek court orders or claim shared care while providing little reliable practical or financial support. The law should require fair financial contribution, accurate income information and dependable agreed care, with consequences for deliberate non-payment, repeated cancellations, hidden income and abusive court applications. The child\u2019s welfare must always come first.",
        "background": "Amend section 3 of the Children Act 1989 to define enforceable financial and practical duties attached to parental responsibility, with proportionate consequences where a parent who has the ability to contribute persistently and deliberately fails to meet them.",
